{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890190",
      "title": "Functions & Function Types",
      "sourceHash": "e7f1f5832ed0d857acac264994b8fd96c46d195e48e8eb9da2aafce371834b16",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.066,
          "end": 3.366,
          "en": "- [Lecturer] Now, there are a lot of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.366,
          "end": 5.9,
          "en": "other core TypeScript features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.9,
          "end": 8.133,
          "en": "which I do explore in greater detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.133,
          "end": 10.033,
          "en": "in my TypeScript course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.033,
          "end": 13.233,
          "en": "To come to an end here for this introduction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.233,
          "end": 16,
          "en": "so that we can move to our react example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16,
          "end": 19.1,
          "en": "and see how we connect TypeScript with react,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.1,
          "end": 22.833,
          "en": "there are just two last features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.833,
          "end": 24.4,
          "en": "which I wanna cover here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.4,
          "end": 28.1,
          "en": "And that would be functions combined with types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.1,
          "end": 31.4,
          "en": "and then thereafter, generic types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.4,
          "end": 35.833,
          "en": "Let's start with functions and types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.833,
          "end": 38.2,
          "en": "And I'm saying function and types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.2,
          "end": 40.566,
          "en": "because when we work with functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.566,
          "end": 45.433,
          "en": "there are different places where types can be assigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.4,
          "end": 48.2,
          "en": "Let's start by adding a function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.2,
          "end": 51.433,
          "en": "Let's say the add function again which we saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.466,
          "end": 56.133,
          "en": "The add function can get parameters of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.133,
          "end": 59.566,
          "en": "like any function just as I did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.566,
          "end": 63.233,
          "en": "And then for these parameters, we can assign types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.233,
          "end": 67.93299999999999,
          "en": "That's what we saw before here in this first example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.93299999999999,
          "end": 71,
          "en": "Just as we can set types for variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71,
          "end": 74.066,
          "en": "we can also set types for parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.066,
          "end": 77.3,
          "en": "We can make it clear that here we wanna allow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.3,
          "end": 79.3,
          "en": "numbers for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 82.6,
          "en": "And then I can return a plus b.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 85.26599999999999,
          "en": "But with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.26599999999999,
          "end": 89.366,
          "en": "we also have one inferred type here in this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.366,
          "end": 93.6,
          "en": "And do you see where we're using type inference here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.7,
          "end": 98.46600000000001,
          "en": "Well, here in this function, I am returning a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.46600000000001,
          "end": 103.46600000000001,
          "en": "and that tells TypeScript something about the return type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 106.96600000000001,
          "en": "the type of the returned value of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.96600000000001,
          "end": 109.9,
          "en": "And it infers this type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.9,
          "end": 114.1,
          "en": "We can see the type it infers if we hover over add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.1,
          "end": 117.833,
          "en": "Then we see the TypeScript definition of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.833,
          "end": 120.6,
          "en": "and we see that, of course, for the parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.6,
          "end": 121.966,
          "en": "we have the two types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.966,
          "end": 124.833,
          "en": "We set up the number types, but then here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.833,
          "end": 129.333,
          "en": "after this function name and the parameter list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.333,
          "end": 132.333,
          "en": "this colon here, and this type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.333,
          "end": 133.9,
          "en": "that's not coming from us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.9,
          "end": 135.733,
          "en": "We haven't added this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.733,
          "end": 139.86599999999999,
          "en": "Instead that's the inferred return value type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.86599999999999,
          "end": 142.133,
          "en": "TypeScript infers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.133,
          "end": 146.933,
          "en": "So TypeScript knows that here it will get a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.933,
          "end": 150.9,
          "en": "as a return value because it sees that this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.9,
          "end": 154.833,
          "en": "with these parameters which are always of type number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.833,
          "end": 156.766,
          "en": "can only return a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.766,
          "end": 159.9,
          "en": "There's no other value that could be returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.9,
          "end": 164.2,
          "en": "And that's why this number return value is inferred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.2,
          "end": 166.9,
          "en": "We could also explicitly set it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.9,
          "end": 170.633,
          "en": "We can set the return type of a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.633,
          "end": 174.933,
          "en": "by adding a colon after this function parameter list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.933,
          "end": 177.2,
          "en": "and then setting the return type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.2,
          "end": 180.966,
          "en": "like number, or a string, or a union type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.966,
          "end": 182.533,
          "en": "that would also be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.6,
          "end": 187.266,
          "en": "That's something we can do, but just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.266,
          "end": 189.533,
          "en": "if you don't have a reason for doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.533,
          "end": 190.9,
          "en": "you shouldn't do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.9,
          "end": 193.566,
          "en": "TypeScript already infers a type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.566,
          "end": 195.933,
          "en": "And if that's the type you wanna stick to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.933,
          "end": 199.933,
          "en": "then there's no need to explicitly define it yourself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.933,
          "end": 203.3,
          "en": "Still, I wanna mention this, that functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.3,
          "end": 206.6,
          "en": "when we work with types, don't just use types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.6,
          "end": 210.466,
          "en": "for the parameters, but also for the return value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.466,
          "end": 213.666,
          "en": "That's easy to overlook, but it makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.666,
          "end": 218.066,
          "en": "because a function after all does not have just some input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.066,
          "end": 221.9,
          "en": "It also has some output and hence it has a return type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.86599999999999,
          "end": 224.966,
          "en": "Now there is a special return type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.966,
          "end": 227,
          "en": "which is also worth knowing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227,
          "end": 230.133,
          "en": "And for that, let me add a print function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.133,
          "end": 234.4,
          "en": "where I get a value and that could indeed be of type any",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.4,
          "end": 236.9,
          "en": "because the only thing I'll do with that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.9,
          "end": 239.433,
          "en": "is I'll console log it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.433,
          "end": 243.1,
          "en": "So I don't really care about the concrete type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.1,
          "end": 244,
          "en": "of this value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244,
          "end": 245.2,
          "en": "I'm just logging it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.833,
          "end": 249.666,
          "en": "Now one important note about naming this function \"print\" though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.666,
          "end": 254.466,
          "en": "which I unfortunately only discovered after I named the function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.466,
          "end": 258.766,
          "en": "Of course, in JavaScript, there's a built-in \"print\" function already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.766,
          "end": 262.566,
          "en": "so now this function will clash with this built-in function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.6,
          "end": 266.133,
          "en": "and hence if you would try to compile this TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.166,
          "end": 268.566,
          "en": "you would be getting an error because of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.566,
          "end": 273,
          "en": "so maybe just name it \"printOutput\" or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.1,
          "end": 275.433,
          "en": "to avoid that error!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 278.83299999999997,
          "en": "But the important thing about this print function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.83299999999997,
          "end": 283.533,
          "en": "now is that this function does not return anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.533,
          "end": 287.033,
          "en": "It has no return statement and therefore it has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.033,
          "end": 292.033,
          "en": "a special return type called void.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.633,
          "end": 297,
          "en": "Void is basically comparable to nul and undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297,
          "end": 299.966,
          "en": "but it's only used in conjunction with functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.966,
          "end": 304.266,
          "en": "and it means that this function never returns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.266,
          "end": 306.833,
          "en": "So if I wanna work with the returned value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.833,
          "end": 310.6,
          "en": "from that function, I will work with undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.6,
          "end": 314.4,
          "en": "and that's that special wide type for functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.4,
          "end": 317.133,
          "en": "for the return value of functions.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}